---
import { thermalImage } from "../data/images"
---

<section
  id="thermal"
  class="relative bg-inverted py-section palette-surface-primary"
  aria-labelledby="thermal-heading"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-landing px-container-x sm:px-8 xl:px-14">
    <p
      class="reveal mb-6 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-inverted-foreground/50"
    >
      Thermal Budapest
    </p>

    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-5 lg:gap-16">
      <!-- Left: text -->
      <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-32 lg:col-span-2 lg:self-start">
        <h2
          id="thermal-heading"
          class="reveal max-w-heading font-display text-headline-1 font-bold leading-[1.05] text-inverted-foreground"
        >
          Where the City Exhales
        </h2>

        <p
          class="reveal mt-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-inverted-foreground/60 sm:text-lg"
        >
          Budapest sits on top of 120 natural thermal springs. The Romans built
          the first baths here two thousand years ago. The Ottomans expanded
          them. The Austro-Hungarians turned them into palaces. Today, thermal
          bathing is not a tourist attraction — it is a daily rhythm for a city
          that has always understood the relationship between water, stone, and
          time.
        </p>

        <blockquote
          class="reveal mt-8 border-l-2 border-inverted-foreground/10 pl-4"
        >
          <p
            class="font-display text-sm font-bold italic text-inverted-foreground/60"
          >
            "Some cities are visited. Budapest is remembered."
          </p>
        </blockquote>

        <!-- Stats -->
        <div class="reveal mt-12 grid grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div>
            <span
              class="font-display text-headline-2 font-bold text-inverted-foreground/15"
            >
              120
            </span>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-inverted-foreground/40">
              Natural thermal springs
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span
              class="font-display text-headline-2 font-bold text-inverted-foreground/15"
            >
              70M
            </span>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-inverted-foreground/40">
              Liters of thermal water daily
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Right: photo + details -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-3">
        <figure class="reveal">
          <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-sm">
            <img
              src={`${thermalImage.src}&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80`}
              srcset={`${thermalImage.src}&w=600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 600w, ${thermalImage.src}&w=900&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 900w, ${thermalImage.src}&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 1200w`}
              sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 90vw, 720px"
              alt={thermalImage.alt}
              title={`Photo by ${thermalImage.author} on Unsplash`}
              width={thermalImage.width}
              height={thermalImage.height}
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              class="photo-tone aspect-[4/3] w-full object-cover"
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption class="mt-3 text-xs text-inverted-foreground/40">
            Photo by <a
              href={thermalImage.authorUrl}
              class="underline hover:text-inverted-foreground/60"
              rel="noopener">{thermalImage.author}</a
            >
            on <a
              href={thermalImage.unsplashUrl}
              class="underline hover:text-inverted-foreground/60"
              rel="noopener">Unsplash</a
            >
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <!-- Bath details -->
        <div class="mt-12 grid gap-10 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="reveal">
            <h3
              class="font-display text-headline-3 font-bold text-inverted-foreground"
            >
              Szechenyi Baths
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-inverted-foreground/50">
              One of the largest medicinal bath complexes in Europe, built in
              1913 in Neo-Baroque style. Its outdoor pools steam in winter, with
              chess players sitting chest-deep in hot water — one of Budapest's
              most iconic scenes.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-inverted-foreground/30">
              City Park, Pest side — Opened 1913
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="reveal">
            <h3
              class="font-display text-headline-3 font-bold text-inverted-foreground"
            >
              Gellert Baths
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-inverted-foreground/50">
              Built between 1912 and 1918 at the foot of Gellert Hill, this Art
              Nouveau complex features Zsolnay ceramic tiles, marble columns,
              and an elaborate wave pool. Its thermal water has been used for
              healing since the 13th century.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-inverted-foreground/30">
              Gellert Hill, Buda side — Opened 1918
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
